】//!\nL23:     【17†16】//! Let `k` be the folding factor and `ell_zk` the mask code message length.\nL24:     【18†17】//!\nL25:     【19†18】//! 1. Prover samples `k` univariate masks of degree `ell_zk - 1` over the extension field.\nL26:     【20†19】//! 2. The masks are batch encoded under a zero-knowledge code, MMCS-committed\nL27:     【21†20】//!    as one matrix, and absorbed into the Fiat-Shamir transcript.\nL28:     【22†21】//! 3. Prover sends `mu_tilde`, the sum of all mask evaluations over `{0,1}^k`.\nL29:     【23†22】//! 4. Verifier samples a combining challenge `eps` in the extension field.\nL30:     【24†23】//! 5. Per-round wire polynomial mixes:\nL31:     【25†24】//!    - the live mask,\nL32:     【26†25】//!    - past mask evaluations at sampled challenges,\nL33:     【27†26】//!    - future-mask endpoints,\nL34:     【28†27】//!    - the plain sumcheck contribution scaled by `eps`.\nL35:     【29†28】//!\nL36:     【30†29】//! # Round polynomial at a glance\nL37:     【31†30】//!\nL38:     【32†31】//! For round `j` with past challenges `gamma_1, ..., gamma_{j - 1}`:\nL39:     【33†32】//!\nL40:     【34†33】//! ```text\nL41:     【35†34】//!     h_j(X) = 2^{k - j}     * s_j(X)\nL42:     【36†35】//!            + 2^{k - j}     * sum_{l <  j} s_l(gamma_l)\nL43:     【37†36】//!            + 2^{k - j - 1} * sum_{l >  j} ( s_l(0) + s_l(1) )\nL44:     【38†37】//!            + eps           * plain_piece_j(X)\nL45:     【39†38】//! ```\nL46:     【40†39】//!\nL47:     【41†40】//! Verifier checks:\nL48:     【42†41】//!\nL49:     【43†42】//! ```text\nL50:     【44†43】//!     round 1  : h_1(0) + h_1(1) = eps * mu + mu_tilde\n"
